    "explanation": "To both parties: the disputed SGD 3.20 is refunded in full, and it is the whole of the contested amount.\n\nThe fare was an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip (quoted_fare_sgd SGD 22.00 on EV-FARE-09114), so under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were fixed at booking and a longer routing costs the rider nothing on those lines: no distance-or-time refund is payable however large the excess. The only live question is the SGD 3.20 ERP line. The platform's own proximity computation on the GPS trace (EV-GPS-09114) places the vehicle's closest fix 7,482.07 m from the charged 'Bukit Merah Central westbound' gantry, roughly thirty times the 250 m radius POL-RD-09 uses to treat a fix as a crossing; the fare ledger itself carries that same line with on_optimal_route set to false; and the trip record (EV-TRIP-09114) bills SGD 0.00 of optimal-route ERP. The trace is complete for policy purposes (100% coverage, no gap above 30 seconds, max_gap_sec 0.0), so this is not a data failure, and the driver does not contest the crossing. The line is therefore a phantom charge under POL-RD-09(4) — a billing-integrity failure refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists — and it is equally the whole amount by which charged_total (SGD 25.20) exceeds the quote plus properly chargeable pass-throughs (nil: no ERP actually crossed, no tolls, no airport surcharge, waiting_time_fee 0.00) under POL-RD-11(a).\n\nOn the route itself, the trace does establish an excess of 3.5 km / 28.0% (16.0 km trace figure on EV-GPS-09114 against 12.5 km booked optimal on EV-TRIP-09114), which clears POL-RD-01 but is not MATERIAL — below both the 50% and the 8.0 km thresholds — so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not required; in any event deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 610 completed trips, so no repeat pattern is established and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral follows. No driver compensation is due: the rider was billed for exactly the 16.0 km the trace records, so the POL-RD-04 unbilled-distance shortfall is zero, and the chat log carries no rider detour instruction (waypoint_hint null). The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09114-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and is not relied on by any finding; no exculpatory clause was invoked against it. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires — identifiers and timestamps match across the trip record, trace and ledger, the trace is unimpaired, and the only line without a trace counterpart is the one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly carves out — so the disputed amount is not held and no escalation is required.\n\nThe billing-integrity finding is referred for review as above."
