    "confidence": 0.96,
    "explanation": "Both of you agree on the decisive fact, and the platform's own measurements confirm it, so this is a straightforward pass-through correction.\n\nThe receipt on TRP-09114 carried one ERP line: SGD 3.20 for the 'Bukit Merah Central westbound' gantry at (1.34, 103.78). Compared against the trip's GPS trace, the vehicle's closest fix is 7,482 m from that gantry — roughly thirty times the 250 m radius POL-RD-09 uses to treat a fix as a crossing. The fare ledger independently marks the same gantry as not on the optimal route, and the driver's routing snapshot for the booked route carries SGD 0.00 of ERP. The driver's own statement on file ('I did not see or pass the gantry named on the receipt') concedes the same point. Under POL-RD-09(4) a charge for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure and is refunded in full, whether or not any deviation exists. That is the SGD 3.20 you are getting back.\n\nOn the deviation itself: the trace does establish one — 16.0 km driven against a 12.5 km optimal, an excess of 3.5 km (28%), clearing both POL-RD-01 gates and falling short of the MATERIAL thresholds of 50% and 8.0 km, so no POL-RD-06 driver-profile check or conduct referral is triggered (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 610 completed trips in 90 days). But this was an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip: the quoted fare was SGD 22.00 and the charge SGD 25.20, so under POL-RD-11 the distance and time lines were fixed at booking and POL-RD-02 does not run — a longer route cost you nothing on those lines. The only amount by which the charge exceeds the quote plus properly chargeable pass-through lines is the phantom ERP line, so POL-RD-11(a) and POL-RD-09(4) both arrive at the same figure of SGD 3.20, counted once. That is the whole of the contested amount, so the outcome is FULL_REFUND.\n\nNo driver compensation is due: you were billed for exactly the 16.0 km the trace records (distance_charged_km 16.0 against trace_distance_km 16.0), so the POL-RD-04 unbilled-distance limb has no shortfall to work on, and the chat log holds a single message with no detour instruction, so the rider-requested-detour limb cannot run either.\n\nTwo procedural points. First, the trace is not impaired for policy purposes — 100% coverage, no gap above 30 seconds — so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) and POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged, and no independent corroboration beyond the trace is required. Second, EV-ADVIS-09114-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); because it carries no fact I have not relied on it, and its absence simply means no road-closure exoneration is available — nothing turns on that, since no distance refund was available on this fare model in any case. The unmatched ERP line is refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly carves out, so there is no basis to hold the disputed amount pending review. No profile field has been used to establish or deny any fact about this trip; POL-GEN-01 governs how the profiles were treated."
